o pair (8s and 3s) is vulnerable but has showdown value. The opponent has been extremely passive, checking every street and only calling my flop raise. This pattern suggests either a weak hand, a draw, or a trap. Given the flush draw on board and my marginal two-pair, checking accomplishes several goals: (1) Controls pot size with a medium-strength hand, (2) Prevents getting check-raised if opponent is trapping, (3) Allows me to see the river card cheaply and reassess, (4) May induce a bluff on the river from worse hands. Betting would only get called by better hands or draws, making it -EV.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
